0ba9c40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180604 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180605 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180605 #edb/ref 1061 53474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180605 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "51cb3a96-772b-5cf8-a320-e21f950a928a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180605 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180606 #edb/ref 1061 53477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180606 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "01563470-15f3-5ad3-a0d7-68cf371ee42d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180606 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180768 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's remind ourselves of the three rules for dividing with negative numbers:\n\n- A negative number divided by a positive number gives a negative number.\n$(-)\\div(+) = (-)$\n- A positive number divided by a negative number is also a negative number.\n$(+)\\div(-) = (-)$\n- A negative number divided by a negative number is a positive number.\n$(-)\\div(-) = (+)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180768 #edb/ref 1065 8022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180768 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "19bbbf1e-a31e-54b1-92bb-a2fb71bf54b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180768 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180769 #edb/ref 1064 "As an example, let's find the value of\n\n$$\n2.4 \\div (-4)\n$$\n\nDividing a positive number by a negative number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since\n\n$$\n2.4\\div 4=0.6\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n2.4 \\div (-4) = -0.6\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180769 #edb/ref 1065 8023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180769 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3c2ea5e2-fa57-573b-8e38-712b30958ca4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180769 #edb/ref 1067 "A Worked Example" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
